      "code": "LABEL_ERROR",
      "text": "If 'AVOID labels' are subjectively defined or inferred without rigorous validation, they could introduce significant noise or misclassification, making the research question untestable, similar to the issues encountered in FAM:SF-APPA-005."
    }
  ],
  "predicted_outcome": {
    "supported": 0.6,
    "rejected": 0.2,
    "untestable": 0.1,
    "artifact": 0.05,
    "uncertain": 0.05
  },
  "decision": "proceed_with_changes",
  "design": {
    "estimand": "The difference in opponent next-possession Points Per Possession (PPP) after 'our' team runs a specific offensive play type X, compared to a baseline (e.g., opponent PPP after other non-X plays or overall opponent PPP). We will then assess if this difference consistently exceeds a pre-defined threshold to justify an 'AVOID' label for play X.",
    "unit": "An individual opponent offensive possession immediately following 'our' team's offensive possession that concluded with play type X.",
    "sample": "All 'our' team's offensive possessions ending in play type X and the immediately following opponent possessions from NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 regular seasons and playoffs, and NBA 2025-26 regular season (complete) and playoffs (complete as of 2026-06-21).",
    "power": "A power analysis will be conducted to determine the minimum detectable effect size for a given significance level (alpha=0.05) and expected sample sizes for various play types. If initial sample sizes for specific play-type sequences are too small, aggregation across similar play types or further analysis will be considered.",
    "controls": "Statistical controls will include game context variables (score differential, time remaining, quarter/period), player personnel on the court (our team and opponent), opponent quality (as measured by season-long efficiency metrics), the outcome of 'our' preceding possession (e.g., made shot, missed shot, turnover, foul), and home/away status. A regression framework (e.g., mixed-effects model) will be used to account for team and player specific effects.",
    "falsification": "The hypothesis would be falsified if, for a given play type X, the opponent next-possession PPP does not significantly differ from the baseline, or if it consistently falls below the threshold required for an 'AVOID' label, or if the effect is in the opposite direction (i.e., opponent next-possession PPP is *lower* after play X).",
    "multiplicity": "If testing multiple play types, a Bonferroni correction or False Discovery Rate (FDR) control will be applied to adjust p-values for multiple comparisons, especially when identifying 'AVOID' labels.",
    "decision_rule": "A play type X will be designated as driving 'AVOID' labels if its effect on opponent next-possession PPP is statistically significant (p < 0.05 after multiplicity correction) and the magnitude of the increase in opponent PPP consistently exceeds a pre-defined 'AVOID' threshold (e.g., 0.1 PPP or 0.15 PPP above baseline) across seasons and robust to controls. The 'AVOID' threshold will be defined prior to analysis based on domain expertise or historical distributions of PPP changes.",
    "data_version": "NBA 2022-23 to 2025-26 seasons (regular season and playoffs)."
  }
}

